      "stageRecord": "On the supplementary reading, האיש independently identifies a man, and the relative adds that the speaker saw him. Such a reading requires appropriate discourse and supplementary intonation; the absence of written commas does not categorically exclude it. The structural distinction will be DP-level rather than NP-level relative attachment. Initially, D ה and N איש form the definite nominal and jointly realize האיש. In the relative IP, ראיתי takes the overt pronoun אותו as its complement and a silent first-person singular pro as its VP-internal subject. The verb assigns the experiencer role to pro and the theme role to the object, and licenses accusative Case on אותו. The latter is represented as one inflected pronominal terminal. Relative I contains past tense and first-person singular agreement. The matrix verb הלך is still a separate lexical object.",
