      "stageRecord": "The relative verb first raises from V to I, leaving a silent head trace. The silent subject then raises from Spec-VP to Spec-IP, where finite I licenses nominative Case and identifies pro through first-person singular agreement. The relative CP is formed with ש in C and a base-generated silent operator in Spec-CP. This operator A′-binds אותו in its existing object position: the object remains overt, and neither an object gap nor movement from that position is posited. Principle B is respected because the local subject is not coindexed with the object and the operator lies outside the local IP domain. The CP is right-adjoined to the independently referential DP rather than to NP. Its operator is anchored to that DP's referent, producing supplementary information instead of restricting the nominal predicate. The C terminal and the raised relative verb jointly realize שראיתי. The entire DP, including its supplement, is then merged in matrix Spec-VP and receives the theme role from הלך. Matrix finite I is introduced with past tense and third-person masculine singular agreement, before matrix subject raising or verb raising.",
